A||||6||JohnnyK||Most likely the thermostat?||||1||
Z||000000||JohnnyK||11-30-2000||05:21 PM||||After driving for awhile, the temp swings all the way up (almost to the red) then after a few seconds, drops down to way below 220. This is probably the thermostat? Also, I can hear it hissing and spraying a small amount out the thermostat housing. The cap is new, and it never did this before. Could it just be the thermostat isn't sitting quite properly and pushing up against the cap? Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||sqoach||11-30-2000||05:51 PM||||my temp guage does that too.  but my car also overheats so who knows. <P>------------------<BR>sQoaCh||||reg||11
Z||000002||mshill||11-30-2000||06:39 PM||||You will get wild swings like that when you have air pockets in the cooling system.  First,  you have to fix every coolant leak (that hissing sound is the clue).  Then you have to properly burp the cooling system by making sure the backend of the car is slightly higher than the front.  Remove the thermostat cap and remove the stat.  Fill it up.  Replace cap (without stat).  Run engine for a couple of minutes.  Remove cap and top off.  Repeat until you don't need to top it off anymore.  Replace the stat and cap and you are set.  For this to work and so you don't have to do it everyday you drive, make sure that all leaks have been fixed. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||11-30-2000||08:41 PM||||If it's hissing out the cap then the cap isn't sealling. just because it's new doesn't mean it's good. The lip of the thermostat housing could also be messed up. it doesn't take much for that cap to leak.||||reg||1
Z||000004||JohnnyK||11-30-2000||09:05 PM||||Well, it wasn't hissing until I took the thermostat out and then put it back in (unless I just never noticed it before). I should look into that.||||reg||1
Z||000005||rogergarrison||12-01-2000||06:41 PM||||id check the thermostat just since its so ez to do, sounds like you got an air pocket. make sure when u fill it, open the cap on radiator too. when it overflows close that cap first, and the cap on thermostat last.||||reg||1
Z||000006||JohnnyK||12-01-2000||06:46 PM||||Been there, done that when I filled it up. don't think there is an airpocket.||||reg||1
